{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For your people has corrupted itself</b> HaShem said to Moses that they committed two evils. The first: \"For your people has corrupted itself,\" and the meaning of corruption (השחתה) is the demolition of a structure, as it is said: \"and each man with his demolishing tool (כלי משחיתו) in his hand\" (Ezekiel 9:1), \"Behold, I am against you, O destroying mountain (הר המשחית)\" (Jeremiah 51:25), Babylon that demolishes every wall and tower. And the meaning of the corruption here is that which our Rabbis called \"he who cuts down the plantings.\" The second: \"For they have made a molten calf and bowed down to it and sacrificed to it.\" Now the first transgression — only HaShem alone knows it, for He knows the hidden things of the heart, and the second is the deed of those among them who sinned by offering sacrifices, as I have explained. And behold, the majority of the people sinned in the matter of the calf, for so it is written: \"And all the people broke off the golden rings,\" and were it not for this, the wrath would not have been against all of them to destroy them. And behold, those killed and those struck by plague were few, for among the multitude the sin was in evil thought, as I have explained." "And the meaning of <b>that you brought up from the land of Egypt</b> is understood from the verse \"And Moses caused Israel to set out from the Sea of Reeds\" (Exodus 15:22), or He wanted to say to him as they themselves said: \"For this Moses, the man, who brought us up from the land of Egypt\" — and so in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 9:12) \"whom you brought out of Egypt,\" for through you they went out, as they say. But Moses said in his prayer: \"whom You brought out of the land of Egypt with great power and with a mighty hand\" (Exodus 32:11), for You alone are He who brings them out, for Yours is the power and the might, for \"with great power\" — \"Your right hand, O YHWH, glorious in power\" (Exodus 15:6), and \"with a mighty hand\" — \"Your right hand, O YHWH, shatters the enemy\" (Exodus 15:6). And likewise he said: \"in Your great power and in Your outstretched arm\" (Deuteronomy 9:29), as I hinted above (Exodus 15:6, on \"Your right hand\"), by way of the truth concerning the attribute of the Arm."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:19:54.715182876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}